E1 VERDICT  true codim == C_m for all (n,m): True
E1 VERDICT  gap == floor(m^2/4) == a*c for all (n,m): True

======================================================================
E2: EXACT normal-map rank at n=4, m=2 balanced point (expect 3 = C_2, not 4)
======================================================================
rank P = 3  rank Z = 3  rank(P*Z) = 2  (target rank n-m = 2)
EXACT rank of normal-space map (= local codim of V_2 at this point): 3
naive transverse codim would be (n-r)^2 = 2^2 = 4; C_2 = 3
E2 VERDICT  exact local codim = 3 = C_2 (undershoots naive 4): True

======================================================================
E3: EXACT coker(d mu) dim at n=4, m=4 balanced point (expect a*c=4)
======================================================================
rank P = 2  rank Z = 2  rank(P*Z) = 0  (im Z subset ker P => P*Z = 0)
EXACT dim image(d mu) = 12  ; coker dim = 4
expected a*c = 2*2 = 4 = floor(16/4) = 4^2 - C_4 = 4
E3 VERDICT  exact coker(d mu) dim = 4 = 4^2 - C_4: True

======================================================================
W2 OVERALL
======================================================================
E1 (codim=C_m, gap=floor(m^2/4)=a*c): True
E2 (exact normal-map rank = 3 = C_2): True
E3 (exact coker(d mu) dim = 4 = 4^2-C_4): True
W2 PASS: True

[W2] the balanced product-corank codim C_m undershoots naive m^2 by exactly floor(m^2/4) = coker(d mu). m^2 and C_m are distinct for m>=2.
